            <ArticleTitle>Carcinoma arising in a duplicated colon.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>782-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>One case of adenocarcinoma arising in a duplicated transverse colon is presented. Its unusual feature was the site of the carcinoma origin, which was the true colonic segment and not the duplication.</AbstractText>
